# Lichess 36-month Stage 05 + Stockfish through March

This package processes the three extension months whose API enrichment is now
complete:

- 2023-09
- 2026-01
- 2026-03

It performs four operations:

1. Authenticates the completed API month receipts, every compact response
   Parquet, every unit checkpoint, and the corresponding Stage-01 candidate
   Parquet.
2. Freezes the exact `status == timeout` game IDs and uses the recovered
   canonical Stage-05 producer to construct the true behavioral opportunity
   Parquets.
3. Produces compact, typed ZSTD Parquet inputs for Stockfish.
4. Runs Stockfish 18 at 100,000 nodes per position with up to ten one-thread
   worker processes, in resumable 100,000-row parts.

The package makes no API requests. The existing sequential API collection may
continue while this package runs.

## Important concurrency rule

Do not run this while another Stockfish job is active on the same Mac. The
runner checks for existing `stockfish` processes and exits without writing
production evaluations if it finds any. The API job by itself is not a
conflict.

## Expected runtime

- Stage-05 authentication and construction: 30–90 minutes.
- Stockfish pilot: about one minute.
- Stockfish production: approximately 22–28 hours, depending on the number of
  timeout opportunities and sustained engine throughput.
- Total expected wall time: approximately 23–30 hours from zero.
- Restart after checkpoints exist: completed Stage-05 months, prepared input
  Parquets, and 100,000-row Stockfish parts are authenticated and skipped.

Expected additional free space: approximately 15–30 GiB.

## Outputs

Large Parquet products remain on the external SSD under:

```text
/Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness/derived/replication_36m/
```

The runner creates a compact result ZIP and SHA-256 sidecar in:

```text
__PRIVATE_VALUE_1__/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop
```

Upload those two files when the run completes.

